    "sbar": {
      "situation": "Payments on the bank system are flowing again after a bad limit setting was reverted. The payment probe now passes end to end, confirmed by one clean recovery look at 32 s.",
      "background": "The scheduler changed max_transfer_minor on payments from 1000000 to 1, so every payment was refused at payments and at the gateway with '422 amount exceeds transfer limit'. Separately, the screening process exited once with exit code 15 and stopped answering, but this caused no symptom.",
      "assessment": "The incident commander itself reverted max_transfer_minor on payments from 1 back to 1000000, and payments recovered. The commander also failed screening over to its standby and restarted screening; both completed, and screening is now served by its standby.",
      "recommendation": "Find out why the scheduler set max_transfer_minor to 1 and stop it from doing so again. Expect refusal rates to stay high until the pre-revert window ages out. Operations should review the payments refused during the window when the limit was 1, as customers may need to retry them."
    },
